Maker-Breaker Schur hypergraph game | 21 | 4 | cauldrons are bins in a positional game on triples (a,b,a+b)
Collatz two-block residue analogy | 21 | 3 | density is blind when moves arrive in correlated residue blocks
adaptive adversarial cauldrons | 19 | 2 | players choose own/opponent and schedule control becomes PSPACE-like
LRC depth/Helly cauldron analogy | 18 | 1 | boil events mimic retained overlap order rather than scalar density
raw cauldron-label minimax | 13 | 0 | exact for small k but forgets the reusable residue mechanism

